{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-91280-r4518989","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Pad Thai Sauce","sourcePageId":91280,"sourceRevision":"4518989","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-21T17:19:50Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Pad%20Thai%20Sauce&oldid=4518989","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:20:09.094Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Asian recipes","Category:Easy recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for sauces and condiments","Category:Recipes using chile paste and sauce","Category:Recipes using cornstarch","Category:Recipes using fish sauce","Category:Recipes using peanut oil","Category:Recipes using sugar","Category:Recipes using vegetable oil","Category:Recipes with metric units","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:Southeast Asian recipes","Category:Thai recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"5ce4bd4d73dcb0815bdd9c20762a102f53bd42e30f1dbf7ea03e57fa8f4b8e37","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Sauce recipes\n| Difficulty = 2\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Sauces|Sauces]] \n\n'''Pad thai sauce''' is commonly used in a Thai dish that shares the same name. This is a simplified version that is versatile enough to use in many other dishes. This recipe works best with rice noodles and is a great addition to any cook's stir-fry repertoire.\n\n==Ingredients==\n\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]] clove\n* 3 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoons]] [[Cookbook:Vegetable oil|vegetable oil]] (preferably [[Cookbook:Peanut Oil|peanut oil]])\n* 3 tablespoons [[Cookbook:Tamarind|tamarind]] or [[Cookbook:Pineapple|pineapple]] juice\n* 2 tablespoons [[Cookbook:Soy Sauce|soy sauce]]\n* ¼ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] (60 ml) Thai [[Cookbook:Fish Sauce|fish sauce]]\n* ¼ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] (60 ml) [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n* 1 tablespoon sambal oelek chili paste\n* ½ tablespoon [[Cookbook:Cornstarch|cornstarch]]\n\n==Procedure==\n\n# Mince the garlic. Lightly brown it in a [[Cookbook:Frying Pan|frying pan]] over high heat with the oil.\n# Combine the juice, soy sauce, fish sauce, and sugar and mix thoroughly\n# After mixture starts bubbling, add the chili paste and cornstarch. Mix well and cook for another minute or two.\n\n[[Category:Recipes for sauces and condiments|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes_with_metric_units|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Thai recipes]]\n[[Category:Asian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using sugar]]\n[[Category:Southeast Asian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chile paste and sauce]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cornstarch]]\n[[Category:Recipes using fish sauce]]\n[[Category:Recipes using vegetable oil]]\n[[Category:Recipes using peanut oil]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Pad Thai Sauce","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1 garlic clove","sourceText":"1 garlic clove","amountText":"1 garlic clove","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"3 tablespoons vegetable oil (preferably peanut oil)","sourceText":"3 tablespoons vegetable oil (preferably peanut oil)","amountText":"3 tablespoons vegetable oil (preferably peanut oil)","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id"